<title>DENMARK: Danish March trade surplus 2.576 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish March trade surplus 2.576 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 2.576 billion crowns in March 1997, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>It compared to a revised 3.240 billion crowns surplus in February. Seasonally adjusted the surplus was 2.182 billion crowns in March, compared to February's revised 3.323 billion crowns.</p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			   March 1997	Feb 1997    March 1996</p>
<p>Exports		    24.677	   25.100	 25.916</p>
<p>Imports		    21.585	   21.704	 22.557</p>
<p>Trade balance excl ships 2.576	   3.240	  3.438</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>balance excluding ships  2.182	   3.323	  2.858</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average seasonally-adjusted March trade surplus excl. ships of 2.4 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969652</p>
</text>
